{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792502715,"nonce":"Ng0EsdwsIljJyxlhCUtLtsf9cM8=","title":"Snapshot: retain exported generic templates for importing callers","message":"Shared snapshot audit for TypeScript modules found a concrete template-retention gap. lower_for_snapshot_releasing calls lower::lower_typed_program, which calls monomorphize_module. That pass moves every generic function out of the module into a temporary context and restores only instantiated concrete bodies. A generic exported by a library without local concrete calls therefore has no template left in the returned HIR. SnapshotBuilder::module_lowered then strips TypedFunction bodies from the interface/artifact. A later importing program cannot instantiate that export for its own concrete types.\n\nPreserve exported generic templates separately from executable concrete functions, or retain a supported template representation in the snapshot. Decode templates only when requested, instantiate through shared cached HIR monomorphization, and never execute an opaque T body. Do not solve this by reparsing/re-lowering every dependency or cloning the whole snapshot at each call.\n\nAcceptance: snapshot a generic identity and a generic array reader with no local instantiations; import them into a fresh program/runtime and specialize for native integer, float, boolean and string elements. Verify nonzero-index typed GEP stride/alignment, duplicate-instance reuse, static ownership and interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM/mixed-tier execution. Include an unused generic export that remains encoded and make whole-program use/standalone-library packaging semantics explicit.\n\nThe implementation-path finding is from code inspection; current snapshot tests cover concrete functions, not exported generic templates. Keep this issue open until a cross-snapshot generic execution regression passes.\n\nBlocks TypeScript module/snapshot integration: 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564. Parent compatibility: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5. This differs from the existing ZynML type-argument inference issue.","files":null}]}